phase P1
title Static foundation

tasks
    T101
        title        Build exact Definition grammar and identity
        status       open
        priority     medium
        derives_from [@plan.Statecharts.O1, @plan.Statecharts.V1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Statecharts.O1]
        description
            Implement the inert Definition value, closed authored-name rules, exact 
            event/input/memory inference, recursive state declarations, and flat operation 
            catalogue fields. Keep construction synchronous and free of runtime work. This 
            establishes the source types consumed by Machine and App compilation.
        acceptance
            Positive and negative type/runtime vectors prove exact literal identity, accepted names 
            and byte lengths, nested states through depth 10, exact events/input/memory, and the 
            one supported memory source. Reject depth 11, malformed or duplicate states, unknown 
            fields, invalid names, malformed payloads, structural event lookalikes, and authored 
            void input before side effects. Construction invokes no initializer, selector, actor, 
            service, storage, or Effect. Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and 
            `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/definition/test/definition.test.ts`; both 
            pass. Write scope: `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/definition/**` and 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/internal/authored-name.ts` plus focused fixtures. 
            Evidence: `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/definition/test/definition.test.ts` and type 
            fixtures.

    T102
        title        Compile the closed recursive Machine grammar
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T101]
        derives_from [@plan.Statecharts.O2, @plan.Statecharts.V2]
        satisfies    [@plan.Statecharts.O2]
        description
            Compile accepted Definition values into inert machine tables with exact recursive 
            states, defaults, paths, event handlers, targets, redirects, reentry, and tokens. 
            Consume the nominal Definition from T101 without decoding or validating it again. 
            Runtime turns and continuing work belong to later Tasks.
        acceptance
            Positive and negative type/runtime vectors prove exact state and event inference, 
            recursive paths, direct-child defaults, transition selection, redirects, and reentry. 
            Reject missing, extra, misplaced, duplicate, non-direct, or over-depth nodes before 
            work; prove definition failure is propagated unchanged and the machine callback is not 
            called. Construction invokes no transition callback, actor, Effect, service, or 
            operation. Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/test/machine.test.ts`; both pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/**` and focused fixtures. Evidence: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/test/machine.test.ts` plus compile fixtures.

    T103
        title        Compile the closed application graph and stable identities
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T102, @T106]
        derives_from [@plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O1, @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V1]
        satisfies    [@plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O1]
        description
            Compile ordered modules, exact keyed App.M, immutable application identity, admitted 
            machines and descriptor graph edges. Preserve machine property names and exact 
            authored-name identity from T101/T102. Keep compilation inert and reject graph growth 
            after compilation.
        acceptance
            Positive and negative graph/type vectors prove every listed machine and descriptor 
            contributes to the closed graph and exact requirement traversal. Reject duplicate 
            module IDs, property names, machine values, descriptor ownership collisions, foreign or 
            unadmitted descriptors, and post-compile additions before actor or work creation. ASCII 
            and multibyte app/machine/ref identity vectors use UTF-8 byte lengths and preserve 
            spelling. Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/app/test/app.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/app/test/graph.test.ts`; both pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/app/**` and focused app/type fixtures. Evidence: app 
            and graph tests plus compile fixtures.

    T104
        title        Preserve exact RequirementsOf and Implementation closure
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T103, @T106]
        derives_from [@plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O2, @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V2]
        description
            Implement covariant requirement carriers and inert typed Implementations. Preserve raw 
            descriptor requirements, remove only Flow-owned Scope, and compose the exact machine, 
            module, app, and provider unions. Provider construction remains inert; Runtime 
            acquisition belongs to P2.
        acceptance
            Positive and negative isolated type fixtures prove exact R propagation, covariance, 
            cross-module unions, raw descriptor R, fixture/Story/model carrier preservation where 
            available, and removal of only Flow-owned Scope. Reject missing/surplus/duplicate 
            providers and recursive expansion without excessive instantiation. Provider 
            constructors acquire no services or Scope and preserve success/failure/environment 
            types without assertions. This Task proves the static app/machine/module/Implementation 
            carrier base; Story, fixture, and model carrier closure is checked with their P5 
            owners. Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/implementation/test/implementation.test.ts`; both pass. 
            Write scope: `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/implementation/**`, 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/app/requirements.ts`, and focused type fixtures. App 
            graph ownership remains T103; Story, fixture, and model carrier closure remains with 
            P5. Evidence: implementation tests and compile fixtures.

    T105
        title        Establish canonical Diagnostics and safe rendering
        status       open
        priority     medium
        derives_from [
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O1,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O3,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O4,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O5,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V1,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V3,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V5,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O6
                     ]
        satisfies    [
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O1,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O3,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O4,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O5,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O6
                     ]
        description
            Implement the sole Diagnostic schema, closed usage/diagnostic codes, reusable 
            typed-failure and complete-Cause mapping boundary, FlowUsageError projection, and 
            shared safe renderer. Keep host formatting separate, preserve exact success/environment 
            channels, and retain Failure/Die/Interrupt distinctions until cleanup/evidence 
            aggregation is complete. Persistence and Story/Dispose terminal-error ownership remain 
            with T401, T203, and T508.
        acceptance
            Positive: schema/type fixtures prove exact tags, classifications, fields, finite 
            path/detail domains, closed codes, the 19 maintained usage-remediation rows, and stable 
            FlowUsageError code/path/details. Structural decode translates SchemaError once; 
            semantic validation remains Result data; typed failure mapping preserves A and R. 
            Complete Cause survives cleanup aggregation and classifies defect before typed failure 
            before interruption-only. Check: diagnostic schema/mapping tests, focused Cause tests, 
            and check:types; expected: exact channels and precedence. Failure: reject unknown 
            codes, malformed paths/details, missing fields, non-finite numbers, and unsupported 
            terminal Error projections. Renderer tests cover all classifications and hostile text 
            while excluding raw input, stack, ANSI, fabricated locations, and Cause. Expected: only 
            Failure plus FlowUsageCode becomes FlowUsageError; no Cause escapes. Run nub run 
            --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types and nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/diagnostic/test/diagnostic.test.ts; both pass. Write 
            scope: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/diagnostic/** and focused fixtures. Evidence: 
            schema, mapping/Cause, usage projection, and renderer tests.

    T106
        title        Settle operation types and canonical-key seams
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T101, @T105, @T107]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Transactions.O1,
                     @plan.Transactions.V1,
                     @plan.Resources.O1,
                     @plan.Resources.V1,
                     @plan.Streams.O1,
                     @plan.Streams.V1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2
                     ]
        description
            Implement exact settled descriptor, input, operation-family, and canonical-key types 
            needed by App and Runtime. Keep unresolved resource/stream authoring forms and omitted 
            freshness policy local to their Questions; do not infer aliases, containers, callbacks, 
            or defaults.
        acceptance
            Type fixtures retain exact P/K/A/E/R and transaction states/options across descriptors 
            and consumers; prove canonical-key accepted values, UTF-8 identity and bounds through 
            the shared codec. Reject widened/missing inputs, wrong key/result relationships, 
            unsupported key structures, and extra public methods. Constructor proofs run no 
            adapters or work. This Task owns only the settled operation/key type seam; P3 T306 owns 
            the complete `Transactions.O1`/`V1` proof; `Resources.Q1` and `Streams.Q1`-bound forms 
            remain explicitly assigned to P3 decision/authoring Tasks. Run `nub run --filter 
            flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/operation.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/key.test.ts`; both pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/input.ts`, `key.ts`, `configuration.ts`, 
            `operation.ts`, their focused tests, and canonical-value type fixtures. P3 owns 
            resource/transaction/stream implementations and runtime policy. Evidence: operation/key 
            tests and compile fixtures.

    T107
        title        Build the shared portable structural codec core
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T101, @T105]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2]
        description
            Implement one bounded, portable structural walker and private Schema decoding boundary 
            for persistence and artifact import/export, including canonical UTF-8 handling. Define 
            the initial private evidence-record contract consumed by Runtime; do not add artifact 
            envelopes or duplicate schema owners here.
        acceptance
            Positive and negative byte/structure vectors cover ASCII and multibyte UTF-8, malformed 
            UTF-8, surrogate rejection, exact depth/node/array/string/property-key/byte bounds, 
            malformed JSON, duplicate keys where detectable, cycles, negative zero, non-finite 
            values, and one versus concatenated gzip members. Pass only when malformed or 
            over-bound bytes reject before mutation/work with the bounded failure path and 
            category, canonical bytes are stable across supported hosts, and no Buffer/parser 
            exception/raw Cause leaks. Evidence contract is private and version-neutral at this 
            stage; no public turn/evidence type is added. Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite 
            check:types` and focused tests under `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/wire/tests`; both 
            pass. Write scope: `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/wire/**`, 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/internal/utf8.ts`, and focused fixtures. Evidence: 
            wire tests, byte vectors, and compile fixtures.

    T108
        title        Establish initial routes and close the static-foundation gate
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T103, @T104, @T105, @T106, @T107]
        derives_from [@plan.PackageContract.O1, @plan.PackageContract.O2, @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2]
        description
            Create and verify the initial internal public-surface facades and route/type fixtures 
            used by capability Tasks. Close the P1 static-foundation gate by checking completed 
            predecessor proofs for definitions, machine grammar, App graph, requirements, 
            diagnostics, operation/key seams, and portable codec. Keep route declarations and 
            fixtures local under src/public; T601 alone owns package.json and the four final 
            package entrypoint files. Leave final public absence cleanup and packed-consumer 
            cutover to P6.
        acceptance
            Positive consumer fixtures import the supported internal public facades and their 
            initially owned names. Negative fixtures reject undeclared internal/private names and 
            route cross-contamination. Confirm T101–T107 focused proofs and the pinned compiler 
            fixture pass as the P1 exit gate. The check does not claim final package absence, fresh 
            packed behavior, or cutover. Run `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and 
            `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/public/test/public-routes.test.ts`; both 
            pass. Write scope: `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/public/**` and route/type fixtures 
            only. T601 owns `package.json`, `src/index.ts`, `src/react-entry.ts`, `src/testing.ts`, 
            and `src/inspect.ts`. Evidence: public route tests and compile fixtures.
